ull,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2599765749","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101736#issuecomment-2599765749","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101736","id":2599765749,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6a9Ub1","user":{"login":"L4Vo5","id":37083802,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MDgzODAy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37083802?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/L4Vo5","html_url":"https://github.com/L4Vo5","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L4Vo5/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L4Vo5/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L4Vo5/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L4Vo5/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L4Vo5/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L4Vo5/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L4Vo5/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L4Vo5/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/L4Vo5/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-18T15:49:49Z","updated_at":"2025-01-18T15:49:49Z","body":"> I have improved something similar in the navigation module not so long ago (in 3D). You can see it [here](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/97928). We could do the same thing here. The trick behind this, is that the winding order for the edges and the point all have to be the same sign for it to be inside. It means that you can easily early out with this algorithm, with no branch (other than the return) in the calculations.\r\n\r\nDoesn't that only work for convex polygons?\r\nConsider this concave polygon and the given point. If you trace the polygon clockwise and test the winding order of (start, end, point), most are clockwise, but the spike at the top is counterclockwise\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2e16d7b6-4f3b-427c-b81a-cdf4c1047f7c)\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2599765749/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2599800701","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101736#issuecomment-2599800701","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101736","id":2599800701,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6a9c99","user":{"login":"kiroxas","id":3176062,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNzYwNjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3176062?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas","html_url":"https://github.com/kiroxas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiroxas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-18T17:30:05Z","updated_at":"2025-01-18T20:18:15Z","body":"> Doesn't that only work for convex polygons? \r\n\r\nYes, it does only work for convex. So if the polygons can be any shape for this function, this will not work.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2599800701/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3073832942","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101736#issuecomment-3073832942","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101736","id":3073832942,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc63Nvfu","user":{"login":"mthaddon","id":4114742,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMTQ3NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4114742?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mthaddon","html_url":"https://github.com/mthaddon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mthaddon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mthaddon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mthaddon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mthaddon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mthaddon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mthaddon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mthaddon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mthaddon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mthaddon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-15T14:23:40Z","updated_at":"2025-07-15T14:23:40Z","body":"This worked great for my situation too (documented on https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/82305). Can I suggest adding a test that was failing with the old code but works with this new code?\r\n\r\n```\r\ndiff --git a/tests/core/math/test_geometry_2d.h b/tests/core/math/test_geometry_2d.h\r\nindex 415912fe9e..7b6f2b967b 100644\r\n--- a/tests/core/math/test_geometry_2d.h\r\n+++ b/tests/core/math/test_geometry_2d.h\r\n@@ -101,6 +101,16 @@ TEST_CASE(\"[Geometry2D] Point in polygon\") {\r\n                Vector2 midpoint((p1 + p2) * 0.5);\r\n                CHECK(Geometry2D::is_point_in_polygon(midpoint, p));\r\n        }\r\n+\r\n+       // Test that was failing per https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/82305\r\n+       Vector<Vector2> q;\r\n+       q.push_back(Vector2(300.90625, 193.078125));\r\n+       q.push_back(Vector2(308.2608642578125, 186.9492797851562));\r\n+       q.push_back(Vector2(368.38134765625, 213.6694946289062));\r\n+       q.push_back(Vector2(334.2058715820312, 214.4832000732422));\r\n+       q.push_back(Vector2(305.8999938964844, 203.6999969482422));\r\n+       q.push_back(Vector2(299.3311767578125, 198.5909118652344));\r\n+       CHECK_FALSE(Geometry2D::is_point_in_polygon(Vector2(228, 143), q));\r\n }\r\n \r\n TEST_CASE(\"[Geometry2D] Polygon clockwise\") {\r\n```","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3073832942/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3661026509","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101736#issuecomment-3661026509","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101736","id":3661026509,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7aNtTN","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-16T15:07:24Z","updated_at":"2025-12-16T15:07:24Z","body":"(GitHub ate my review-comment... 😕)\r\n\r\nMakes sense, looks good to me. Thanks!\r\n\r\nTested against current `master` (v4.6.beta.custom_build [5cb1ec590]), confirmed it fixes all reported buggy cases:\r\n- https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/81042#issue-1868498559\r\n\r\n<details><summary>(but I've tested all integer-only points on the square edges instead)</summary>\r\n<p>\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\n@tool\r\nextends EditorScript\r\n\r\nfunc _run() -> void:\r\n\tvar errors_count := 0\r\n\tfor i in range(1,100):\r\n\t\tvar false_values := []\r\n\t\tvar square:PackedVector2Array = [Vector2(-i,-i),Vector2(i,-i),Vector2(i,i),Vector2(-i,i)]\r\n\t\tfor corner in square:\r\n\t\t\tif Geometry2D.is_point_in_polygon(corner, square) == false:\r\n\t\t\t\tfalse_values.append(corner)\r\n\t\tfor j in range(-i + 1, i):\r\n\t\t\tfor edge_point: Vector2 in [\r\n\t\t\t\tVector2(j, -i),\r\n\t\t\t\tVector2(j, i),\r\n\t\t\t\tVector2(i, j),\r\n\t\t\t\tVector2(-i, j),\r\n\t\t\t]:\r\n\t\t\t\tif Geometry2D.is_point_in_polygon(edge_point, square) == false:\r\n\t\t\t\t\tfalse_values.append(edge_point)\r\n\t\tif not false_values.is_empty():\r\n\t\t\tprints(i, false_values)\r\n\t\terrors_count += false_values.size()\r\n\tprint(\"Errors total: %d\" % [errors_count])\r\n```\r\nBefore:\r\n```\r\n36 [(1.0, -36.0)]\r\n37 [(-1.0, -37.0), (-37.0, 1.0)]\r\n38 [(-38.0, 1.0)]\r\n39 [(-39.0, 1.0)]\r\n42 [(-42.0, 0.0), (1.0, -42.0)]\r\n43 [(-1.0, -43.0), (-43.0, -1.0), (0.0, -43.0), (-43.0, 0.0), (1.0, -43.0), (-43.0, 1.0)]\r\n44 [(0.0, -44.0)]\r\n45 [(-45.0, 0.0)]\r\n46 [(0.0, -46.0), (-46.0, 0.0), (1.0, -46.0)]\r\n47 [(-47.0, 0.0)]\r\n48 [(0.0, -48.0)]\r\n49 [(-49.0, -1.0), (0.0, -49.0), (-49.0, 0.0), (1.0, -49.0), (-49.0, 1.0)]\r\n51 [(-1.0, -51.0), (0.0, -51.0), (-51.0, 0.0)]\r\n53 [(-1.0, -53.0), (0.0, -53.0)]\r\n54 [(0.0, -54.0), (-54.0, 0.0), (1.0, -54.0)]\r\n55 [(1.0, -55.0)]\r\n56 [(-1.0, -56.0), (0.0, -56.0)]\r\n57 [(-57.0, -1.0), (-57.0, 0.0), (-57.0, 1.0)]\r\n58 [(-58.0, 0.0)]\r\n59 [(-59.0, -1.0), (-59.0, 0.0), (-59.0, 1.0)]\r\n60 [(-1.0, -60.0), (-60.0, -1.0), (0.0, -60.0), (1.0, -60.0), (-60.0, 1.0)]\r\n61 [(-1.0, -61.0), (0.0, -61.0), (-61.0, 0.0), (1.0, -61.0)]\r\n62 [(-1.0, -62.0), (1.0, -62.0)]\r\n63 [(-63.0, 0.0), (-63.0, 1.0), (2.0, -63.0)]\r\n64 [(-1.0, -64.0)]\r\n65 [(0.0, -65.0), (2.0, -65.0)]\r\n66 [(-66.0, -1.0), (0.0, -66.0), (-66.0, 0.0), (-66.0, 1.0)]\r\n68 [(0.0, -68.0), (-68.0, 0.0)]\r\n69 [(-1.0, -69.0), (0.0, -69.0), (-69.0, 0.0), (1.0, -69.0)]\r\n70 [(0.0, -70.0), (-70.0, 0.0)]\r\n71 [(-1.0, -71.0), (-71.0, -1.0), (1.0, -71.0), (-71.0, 1.0), (2.0, -71.0)]\r\n72 [(0.0, -72.0), (1.0, -72.0), (2.0, -72.0)]\r\n73 [(-2.0, -73.0), (-1.0, -73.0)]\r\n74 [(-2.0, -74.0), (0.0, -74.0), (-74.0, 2.0)]\r\n75 [(-75.0, -2.0), (-1.0, -75.0), (-75.0, -1.0), (-75.0, 0.0), (-75.0, 1.0), (2.0, -75.0), (-75.0, 2.0)]\r\n76 [(-76.0, -1.0), (-76.0, 0.0), (1.0, -76.0), (-76.0, 1.0), (-76.0, 2.0)]\r\n77 [(0.0, -77.0), (-77.0, 0.0)]\r\n78 [(0.0, -78.0), (-78.0, 0.0), (-78.0, 2.0)]\r\n79 [(-79.0, -2.0), (2.0, -79.0)]\r\n80 [(-1.0, -80.0), (-80.0, -1.0), (1.0, -80.0), (-80.0, 1.0)]\r\n81 [(-81.0, -2.0), (0.0, -81.0), (3.0, -81.0), (-81.0, 3.0)]\r\n82 [(1.0, -82.0)]\r\n83 [(-3.0, -83.0), (0.0, -83.0), (1.0, -83.0)]\r\n84 [(-3.0, -84.0), (-84.0, -1.0), (-84.0, 0.0), (-84.0, 1.0), (2.0, -84.0), (-84.0, 3.0)]\r\n85 [(-1.0, -85.0), (-85.0, 0.0), (1.0, -85.0)]\r\n86 [(-2.0, -86.0), (-86.0, -2.0), (-1.0, -86.0), (0.0, -86.0), (-86.0, 0.0), (1.0, -86.0), (2.0, -86.0), (-86.0, 2.0)]\r\n87 [(-2.0, -87.0), (-87.0, -1.0), (0.0, -87.0), (-87.0, 0.0), (-87.0, 1.0)]\r\n88 [(-1.0, -88.0), (-88.0, -1.0), (0.0, -88.0), (1.0, -88.0), (-88.0, 1.0)]\r\n89 [(-2.0, -89.0), (-89.0, -1.0), (0.0, -89.0), (-89.0, 1.0)]\r\n90 [(-90.0, 0.0), (1.0, -90.0)]\r\n91 [(-3.0, -91.0), (-91.0, -3.0), (-1.0, -91.0), (0.0, -91.0), (-91.0, 0.0), (1.0, -91.0), (-91.0, 3.0)]\r\n92 [(-3.0, -92.0), (-92.0, -1.0), (0.0, -92.0), (-92.0, 0.0), (1.0, -92.0), (-92.0, 1.0), (2.0, -92.0)]\r\n93 [(-2.0, -93.0), (-93.0, -2.0), (-93.0, -1.0), (-93.0, 0.0), (1.0, -93.0), (-93.0, 1.0), (-93.0, 2.0)]\r\n94 [(-1.0, -94.0), (-94.0, -1.0), (-94.0, 0.0), (-94.0, 1.0)]\r\n95 [(-2.0, -95.0), (-95.0, -2.0), (-1.0, -95.0), (-95.0, -1.0), (0.0, -95.0), (1.0, -95.0), (-95.0, 1.0), (2.0, -95.0), (-95.0, 2.0), (3.0, -95.0)]\r\n96 [(-1.0, -96.0), (-96.0, -1.0), (0.0, -96.0), (-96.0, 1.0)]\r\n97 [(-97.0, -1.0), (-97.0, 0.0), (-97.0, 1.0), (2.0, -97.0), (3.0, -97.0)]\r\n98 [(-98.0, -2.0), (0.0, -98.0), (-98.0, 0.0), (1.0, -98.0), (2.0, -98.0), (-98.0, 2.0)]\r\n99 [(-1.0, -99.0), (-99.0, -1.0), (1.0, -99.0), (-99.0, 1.0)]\r\nErrors total: 203\r\n```\r\nAfter:\r\n```\r\nErrors total: 0\r\n```\r\n\r\n</p>\r\n</details> \r\n\r\n- https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/81042#issuecomment-3658399831 / https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114065#issue-3732941433\r\n- https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/82305#issue-1911536593\r\n\r\n<details><summary>(ported to GDScript)</summary>\r\n<p>\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nextends Node2D\r\n\r\nfunc _ready() -> void:\r\n\tvar radius: int = 40\r\n\tvar height: int = 100\r\n\tvar center: Vector2 = Vector2(radius, height * 0.5)\r\n\tvar vertices = Capsule(center, radius, height)\r\n\r\n\tif Geometry2D.is_point_in_polygon(Vector2(29, 16), vertices):\r\n\t\tprinterr(\"Error found in Geometry2D.IsPointInPolygon\")\r\n\r\nstatic func Capsule(center: Vector2, radius: float, height: float) -> PackedVector2Array:\r\n\tvar vertexCount: int = ceili(PI * radius)\r\n\tvar vertices := PackedVector2Array()\r\n\r\n\t# Bottom of the capsule\r\n\tfor i in vertexCount + 1:\r\n\t\tvar phi: float = PI / vertexCount * i\r\n\t\tvar v: Vector2 = Vector2(cos(phi), sin(phi)) * radius\r\n\t\tv.y += center.y + height * 0.5\r\n\t\tv.x += center.x\r\n\t\tvertices.push_back(v)\r\n\r\n\t# Top half-circle of the capsule\r\n\tfor i in range(vertexCount, -1, -1):\r\n\t\tvar phi: float  = -PI / vertexCount * i\r\n\t\tvar v: Vector2 = Vector2(cos(phi), sin(phi)) * radius\r\n\t\tv.y += center.y - height * 0.5 + 2 * radius\r\n\t\tv.x += center.x;\r\n\t\tvertices.push_back(v);\r\n\r\n\treturn vertices\r\n```\r\n\r\n</p>\r\n</details> \r\n\r\n- https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/82305#issuecomment-1733782876\r\n- https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/82305#issuecomment-2620698857\r\n- https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/82305#issuecomment-2648871204\r\n- https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/82305#issuecomment-3069318315","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3661026509/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]